# Asher Project State

Asher is a mod manager for Dust: An Elysian Tail. The frontend is an **Electron** app (`Asher.Electron`). The backend is a C# console process (`Asher.Host`) communicating over **JSONL on stdin/stdout**.

## Completed (do not reimplement)

- Electron shell: sidebar, home hub, settings, patch manager, game setup
- Install / uninstall / launch flows through JSONL contract
- Localization (en-US, pt-BR, es) in renderer `localization.js`
- Theme (Light / Dark) in renderer `theme.js`
- Material Symbols Outlined icons (self-hosted font, `icons.js`)
- Settings auto-save, preference-only reset, browse path
- Install Finish UX with optional launch + minimize
- Install always creates a game backup (`BackupEnabled` forced true; no Settings toggle)
- `setModEnabled` validates mod existence in `PatchManagerService`
- Incremental mod-list rendering (no full DOM rebuild on toggle)
- Toast notifications (`action-banner.js`, top-right stack)
- `markInstalled` / `markUninstalled` contract methods (replaced fragile settings merge)
- Install payload bundled via MSBuild (`install-payload/` beside `Asher.Host.exe`)
- Zip + unpacked Distribution packaging (`npm run dist` → `Distribution/`; GitHub publish via `npm run publish` + `private/GH_TOKEN`)
- Manager UI runs from Distribution only (no deploy into `game/Asher/Asher.App/`)
- Emergency uninstall helper installed as `Uninstall-Asher.cmd` (+ `.ps1`) beside `DustAET.exe` for recovery without the UI
- Settings Removal: Safe uninstallation (in-app) and Total exclusion (launches game-folder `Uninstall-Asher.cmd`)
- GitHub Releases update check / zip apply for the Distribution app (Settings → Check for updates)
- Cross-platform platform abstraction: `IPlatformInfo` + `IGameFolderDiscovery` / `IGameExecutableLayout` / `IRuntimeDeployment` / `IGameProcessLauncher`, Windows implementations, Linux initial stubs (`Asher.Services/Platform`)
- `getPlatformInfo` JSONL method + renderer `platform.js` capability gating (Windows-only removal UI hidden on Linux)
- Host-side projects (`Asher.Core`, `Asher.Services`, `Asher.Host`) target `net8.0` (was `net8.0-windows`)
- Cross-platform path/log baseline: canonical log folder `Asher/AsherLogs` (managed `RuntimeBootstrap` default aligned), Linux settings under `$XDG_CONFIG_HOME/Asher` (fallback `~/.config/Asher`), Linux portable settings only with a `portable` marker
- `Asher.Services.Tests` xUnit project for platform/path units
- Linux game discovery: XDG Steam roots + multiple `libraryfolders.vdf` libraries, best-effort Heroic/Lutris (verified paths only), shared `SteamLibraryVdf` parser; Windows discovery behavior unchanged
- Explicit install-state contract: `InstallStateDto` (`state`/`canUninstall`/`canRestore`/`marker`) via `getInstallState`; renderer uses it instead of inferring from `hasRestorableBackup`; platform-aware `AsherPaths` overloads take `IPlatformInfo`
- Linux runtime deployment: bootstrap + managed runtime + default mods into `Asher/`, `install.json` manifest (schema/version/ELF arch incl. mismatch warning), idempotent deploy, `Mods`/`DefaultMods` payload reconciliation; Linux `HasRestorableBackup = false`; uninstall removes Asher files without touching `DustAET`
- Linux launch: `LinuxGameProcessLauncher` starts `<game>/DustAET` with `UseShellExecute=false`, preserved parent env, `LD_PRELOAD`/`MONO_PATH` prepend + `ASHER_HOME`/`ASHER_MODS_PATH`/`ASHER_LOG_PATH`/`ASHER_PROFILE`; `IProcessStarter` + `IEnvironmentProvider` abstractions (fakeable); incomplete install rejected; Windows shell launch unchanged
- Electron lifecycle uses `getInstallState` + `platform` capabilities (no `hasRestorableBackup` derivation); Windows-only recovery/updater paths gated (`supportsRecoveryHelper`, `process.platform`); `manager-paths.js` platform-aware executable name; updater reports `unavailable` off Windows; `npm run smoke:platform` added
- Linux build/packaging (x64): conditional `PlatformTarget` (x86 only when `Platform == x86`; keying on `RuntimeIdentifier` mis-built `Asher.Services` as x86 and broke the x64 Host); `build:host:linux` self-contained publish with `-p:InvariantGlobalization=true` (no system libicu required); `stage-linux-payload.mjs` (fail-fast) staging `Asher.Linux/out` → `install-payload/DefaultMods`; electron-builder `linux` AppImage + tar.gz with `Asher` executable; `verify-linux-package.mjs`; Windows targets unchanged
- WSL2 validation: Host runs on Linux; install/launch/uninstall/reinstall/partial-repair and Steam/XDG/manual discovery verified against the native Dust install
- Linux launch stdout isolation: game `stdout`/`stderr` are redirected and pumped to the Host `stderr` (`[game-stdout]`/`[game-stderr]`), keeping the JSONL channel clean; Electron logs Host stderr to the manager diagnostic log; `AsherLogs/runtime_*.log` unaffected

## Linux preparation (foundation only)

- No Linux installer implementation yet; Linux platform contracts are initial stubs (`docs/Cross-Platform-Architecture.md`)
- Deferred: Linux install flow/payload staging, `net8.0` host packaging on Linux, bootstrap timing fix, shell recovery helper

## Retired (do not recreate)

- WPF UI: `Asher.App`, `Asher.UserInterface`, `Asher.Localization` — deleted
- WPF-only services: `ManagerLaunch`, `Shortcut`, `InstallationState`, `NavigationItemsManager` (manager deploy/relaunch restored in Electron main, not those C# services)
- `PrepareDistribution.ps1` — WPF-era packaging script
- Prism / MaterialDesign / WPF dependencies in `Asher.Core`
- Portable-as-primary packaging (replaced by zip / Distribution folder)

## Deferred

- Full install wizard stepper chrome
- Content patcher UI (no backend exists)
- Desktop shortcut creation after install

